<TeXmacs|2.1.5>

<style|tmdoc>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|Fonts, from selection to glyph>

  This chapter describes how <TeXmacs> turns the font you asked for into the
  glyphs you see on the screen and in your printed documents. It explains
  how to select a font from the dialogs and how to do the same thing from
  markup or from <scheme>, which files decide what a font name means,
  and how the virtual fonts let <TeXmacs> draw characters which no font on
  your system provides.

  <\traverse>
    <branch|Selecting fonts|font-selection.en.tm>

    <branch|From markup to glyph|font-resolution.en.tm>

    <branch|The font configuration files|font-config.en.tm>

    <branch|Virtual fonts|virtual-fonts.en.tm>
  </traverse>

